<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="164" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Add line: a reviewer adds a line the firm did not bill (BFF route, Invoice Review form, New Billing Event hidden)</title>
    <phase>4 Review (EB-D-188; the number 160 is taken by the end-to-end seam tests)</phase>
    <gate>164a: Q1-Q4 answered in the decisions log, and 095d-0 (InvoiceFirmGate) merged into work. 164c -Apply: Q6 answered and the owner's live go.
      (notes/add-line-brief.md section 4)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>A new write path for invoice lines (app identity, caller rights on the invoice); it changes totals (I-1) and the Decision Record catalog; it writes Signals and the field-secured findings JSON.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus (164a); sonnet (164b, 164c)</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>164a combines access, a totals invariant, 101's findings diff, the Signal episode rules and concurrency. 164b and 164c copy existing patterns.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>164a edits InvoiceCorrectionReevaluation.cs (extraction only), InvoiceTotalsCalculator.cs, DecisionActionCatalog.cs and InvoiceLineReviewEndpoints.cs (095d-0 edits it too). InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs is NOT edited, which avoids overlap with 082d and 095d-2a. 164c can run beside 164a.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>095d-0 (InvoiceFirmGate); 100, 101, 102, 103 (merged)</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ebilling, auth, code-page, ribbon, signals, decision-record</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3 days: 164a 2 days, 164b 0.5 days, 164c 0.5 days; one agent each</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Binding brief, read it first; it is not restated here: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/add-line-brief.md.
    - Section 2 is the closed requirement set (R1-R19, each with its source).
    - Section 3 is the design and the order of writes.
    - Section 4 holds the open questions and their recommendations.
    - Sections 5-11 give the files, the justification, the ADRs, the tests, the limits, the rigor and the split.
    If the brief and a source disagree, the source wins: stop and say which.
    The uac-r2 access conditions (A1-A5) and the ontology-r1 conditions (O1-O3) are binding and appear below as acceptance criteria.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: Finance write paths (line decisions, adjustments, the corrections re-evaluation), the billing Decision Record, Signals, and the Invoice Review code page.</role>

  <goal>POST /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/lines adds one Fee or Expense line to an invoice that is In Review and has a firm.
    - Rights: the caller's Write on the invoice is asked as the caller.
    - The write: the app identity creates the line.
    - The line: Flagged, marked reviewer-added, and outside the firm's billed total.
    - Checks: its rules and the invoice-level total rules run through 101's before/after diff, and the Signals follow D-201.
    - The record: one add-line Decision Record names the caller and the reason.
    The Invoice Review page gets an Add line form. A script hides the model-driven New Billing Event.</goal>

  <scope>
    <in>The route and its DTO; InvoiceLineAddService; the extraction of CRE's request builder and patch helpers; the totals change for Q1; the add-line code (Q3); provenance.source and ReviewLineDto.ReviewerAdded; the DI line; the guard and ledger texts; the client form, button and badge; the ribbon shell, the hides and the script; tests per brief section 8; task notes notes/164-add-line.md.</in>
    <out>Any new Dataverse column or table; any edit to the persister; an AI call (Q4); any external route or projection (Q5, task 130); any edit to uac-r2's child-record route or SecureChild ribbon (Q6); running the ribbon script with -Apply; live writes; bulk add.</out>
  </scope>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="brief R1, R2, R17; uac A2, A4">
      - The route goes in the existing /api/finance group (RequireAuthorization, RequireInternalFinanceCaller) with AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter("ebilling.invoice.decide", InvoiceEntitySet, "invoiceId") and RequireEbillingEnabled.
      - The caller's rights are asked on the INVOICE as the caller, fail closed.
      - The line is written by the app identity.
      - The decider is ResolveCallerSystemUserIdAsync of the caller's own token. Nothing in the body names a person, a total or a status.</constraint>
    <constraint source="brief R3; EB-D-185; uac A3; ont O1">Order: the shape checks (400) come first, before any read. In Review and InvoiceFirmGate are checked BEFORE any write and before any SignalWriter, recorder or set-store call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="brief R6, R15; CRE remarks">
      - Rules run only through the extracted CRE builder and the pure Evaluate, never a copy. The existing correction suites pass unchanged; that is the refactor proof.
      - A stored Blocked entry and the override stamp are never changed.
      - No 073 runs; nothing rejects or holds.
      - A new Procedure gap is 409.</constraint>
    <constraint source="brief R8; D-100; ont O3; uac A5">
      - The Decision Record is written only through BillingDecisionRecorder.RecordAsync (WriteBillingDecisionAsync), after the line write.
      - Preflight runs before any write.
      - The reason is required, at most 2000 characters.
      - ResolvedSignalIds is empty.
      - Facts hold ids and codes only: no description, no name, no free text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="brief R7, R9; ont O2, O3; D-201 Q2">
      - Signals are written through SignalEpisodeLifecycle and SignalWriter with the D-13 key.
      - A changed reason set is Superseded, record-free, followed by episode n+1. An unchanged set refreshes sprk_lastevaluated only.
      - LinkConditionClearedRecordAsync (resolvedBy = the caller) is used only when this decision removed the last open hold reason (InvoiceOpenHolds non-empty before, empty after).</constraint>
    <constraint source="brief R13, R14">
      - The line id and decision id are derived from (invoice, requestId).
      - The per-invoice lock LockKeyFor is taken.
      - ONE commit transaction: the create, plus the submission findings update, plus an invoice update, both IfRowVersionMatches.
      - From the commit on, CancellationToken.None.
      - Every later step is idempotent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q2; CLAUDE.md 11">The marker is provenance.source = "reviewer" inside the existing sprk_extractionconfidence (if the owner confirms Q2). Never a new column without escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md 10; bff-extensions">
      - Placement: the BFF; request-scoped, no job (ADR-052). One AddScoped in FinanceModule. No package.
      - Measure the publish delta against a fresh master build.
      - Logs carry ids and counts only (ADR-015).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ribbon-edit skill; Deploy-EbillingBillingExportRibbon.ps1">
      - The script is a dry run by default. -Apply runs a scoped PublishXml (never PublishAllXml), then the -Verify check. -Verify is read-only.
      - The import replaces the table's RibbonDiffXml, so the dry run refuses when the checked-in diff carries ids that are not live, which includes uac 147's sprk.SecureChild.* (Q6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No live writes. Access defects: the defect and its location only. Wording in commits, the PR and notes describes the change.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <relevant-files>
    <file role="create">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceLineAddService.cs</file>
    <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceLineReviewEndpoints.cs (route, AddLineRequest, result mapping)</file>
