    <file role="modify">Services/Finance/InvoiceTotalsCalculator.cs, InvoiceTotalsService.cs (Q1); Submission/ExtractionProvenance.cs; InvoiceReviewReadService.cs (ReviewLineDto.ReviewerAdded)</file>
    <file role="modify">Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionCatalog.cs; Services/Signals/DecisionRecordWriter.cs:1256 (Q3, ontology sign-off); Submission/SignalEpisodeLifecycle.cs (SignalLogContext.AddLine); Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs; Services/Dataverse/ParentLineage.cs (text)</file>
    <file role="modify">src/solutions/InvoiceReview/src/components/Dialogs.tsx, InvoiceReviewPage.tsx, LinesGrid.tsx; src/services/invoiceReviewApi.ts, reviewModel.ts</file>
    <file role="create">scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingBillingEventRibbon.ps1; infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/BillingEventRibbons/ (Other/Solution.xml, Other/Customizations.xml, Entities/sprk_billingevent/Entity.xml)</file>
    <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_BillingEvent/RibbonDiff.xml (HideCustomActions)</file>
    <file role="reference">InvoiceAdjustmentService.ApplyAddAsync (:451-582); InvoiceLineDecisionService RunAsync/ApplyAsync (:274-318, :617-704); InvoiceCorrectionService.RederiveAsync (:568-660); scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingBillingExportRibbon.ps1; Dialogs.tsx CorrectValueModal</file>
    <file role="modify">tests: tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/InvoiceLineReviewEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs; new tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/InvoiceLineAddServiceTests.cs; InvoiceTotalsCalculatorTests; tests/Spaarke.ArchTests RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs, FindingsJsonAppOnlyReadGuardTests, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests; tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionActionCatalogTests.cs; DecisionRecordWriterTests.Billing.cs; src/solutions/InvoiceReview/src/__tests__</file>
  </relevant-files>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step id="164a-0">Confirm that Q1-Q4 are answered in the decisions log and that 095d-0 is merged. Otherwise STOP.</step>
    <step id="164a">Build the BFF per brief section 3: extraction, service, route, totals, code, marker, guards, and tests T, N, S and G.
      - Run code-review and adr-check.
      - Two adversarial passes.
      - uac-r2 reviews the route (A1-A5); ontology-r1 reviews R7-R9.
      - Measure the publish delta.</step>
    <step id="164b">The client per brief section 3 and R19: AddLineModal on FormModal, the Add line button in the lines toolbar, the reviewer-added badge, and addLine with one requestId kept across Repeat. Then C1-C4, code-review and the npm build.</step>
    <step id="164c">The ribbon shell, the five hides and the script with dry run, -Apply and -Verify. Then P1-P2 and a dry run against dev (read-only). -Apply waits for Q6 and the owner's go.</step>
    <step>Write notes/164-add-line.md: what landed, deviations, the answers Q1-Q7, known limits K1-K6, and the publish delta.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Happy path, Fee and Expense (T1, T2):
      - one sprk_billingevent row, created by the app identity, owner from IRecordOwnershipResolver;
      - sprk_createdbyperson = the caller;
      - the invoice's core and resolver fields, its confirmed firm and currency;
      - sequence = the maximum over all lines + 1;
      - status Flagged, the line finding line.reviewer_added, provenance.source = "reviewer";
      - totals stored per Q1;
      - 200 with lineId, decisionId and totals.</criterion>
    <criterion>The Decision Record (uac A5, ont O3):
      - exactly one record: action add-line, subject the new line;
      - the decider is the caller (BillingDecider.Human), and the reason is stored;
      - ResolvedSignalIds is empty;
      - its facts contain ids and codes only;
      - it is written only through BillingDecisionRecorder, and only after the line write.</criterion>
    <criterion>Rules and Signals (ont O2):
      - a rule on the new line raises a Signal keyed {policy}|sprk_billingevent|{lineId}|1;
      - a changed invoice-level reason set gives Superseded (no sprk_decisionrecord) and then episode n+1;
      - must-not-fire: an unchanged set keeps the same Signal and refreshes only sprk_lastevaluated;
      - a cleared non-hold group is closed ConditionCleared and record-free.</criterion>
    <criterion>The hold link (ont Q7 ruling): in R1 Add line cannot clear the last hold reason (EB-D-185/190; only Override or the re-run releases a Procedure hold), so NO link code is written. Must-not-fire test: an Add line on a held invoice never calls LinkConditionClearedRecordAsync and never closes a Signal ConditionCleared; a stored Blocked entry and the override stamp are byte-identical after any add. Trigger: a later change that gives Add line a hold-clearing path applies O3 then, under ontology's Q1 conditions.</criterion>
    <criterion>The add-line code (ont Q3 ruling): required reason, Tier2b, Judgement, Reversible, RecordOfTruthImpact, subject = the new line (D-75). (1) Added to the line literal at DecisionRecordWriter.cs ~:1256 and to the exact-set test Billing_C2_* in the SAME commit. (2) In BillingActions only, never the commit-route catalog; a test proves POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision refuses add-line like the other billing codes. (3) Line creation is idempotent on the decision id (deterministic line id, or a lookup by decision id before create); a retry test asserts exactly one line and one record. (4) Excludes empty; reversing an added line is a later disallow-line with its own record.</criterion>
    <criterion>One owner of a NEW line (uac-r2 Q6; CLAUDE.md §17). CREATE-ONLY refusal, NOT the full D-204 writer-only rule: D-96's supported detach / move / re-attach sequence (InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.DetachMoveReattachHint; AccessTableReaderScanTests.cs:73 on master) updates sprk_billingevent through the playbook Update Record node and the output orchestrator, so generic UPDATE must keep working (subject to uac-r2 confirming the create-only form). PRECONDITION: origin/master merged into work/ebilling-r1. (1) A create-only table rule refuses a generic create of sprk_billingevent with record_creation.table_unsupported (the code D-204 uses), at every create enforcement point D-204 uses (RecordCreationService, the chat create tool validate and execute); generic update keeps today's guards (InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard, MappingProtectedColumns). (2) Remove sprk_billingevent from ChildRecordEndpoints CreateTables (:71) and fix the comment (:62-67); expect a textual conflict with fm 049b (secure=true on the same route): whoever merges second resolves. (3) Remove only the "New Billing Event" create from src/client/webresources/js/sprk_secure_child_ribbon.js and its test (secureChildRibbonScript.test.ts:248), keeping every other SecureChild control. (4) Grep every other RecordCreationService caller (chat create tool, decision follow-ons, budget inquiry, Office quick-create) and report none creates a billing event. (5) Tests (uac-r2): a generic create of sprk_billingevent through each create path returns the code with nothing written; must-not-fire: the D-96 re-attach update still succeeds, and a typed writer (a line decision, Add line itself) still writes. (6) Update the guards that name the table as needed (fm list: CoreRecordPairUpdateCheckGuardTests:46,52; ExternalDocumentNarrowingGuardTests:1110; WriterOnlyTablesDeleteGuardTests; FeatureRolePrivilegeGuardTests) and the Repair.cs:674 comment; run the D-204 guard and ArchTests. Dev field-mapping profiles checked 2026-11-06: none targets sprk_billingevent. RecordTableRules and ChildRecordEndpoints are field-mapping code: fm copied on the diff; uac-r2 reviews the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion>Coding (EB-D-192): reviewer-typed codes go through the SAME code validation and guideline rules as an imported line; a line with an invalid code raises the same finding and Signal an imported line would (test).</criterion>
    <criterion>I-2: approve is refused while the added line is Flagged and succeeds once the line is decided. Accept all Clean leaves the added line untouched.</criterion>
    <criterion>Totals (Q1): the billed total never changes. Accept, reduce and disallow on an added line give the Q1 approved total (T8). Disallowing an added line never subtracts from the firm's billed lines.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac A1: RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs names the new route in the InvoiceLineReviewEndpoints.cs GovernedFile entry, with its filter and right. OperationAccessPolicy's ebilling.invoice.decide comment lists it. The census test passes.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac A2 (G5): the right is ebilling.invoice.decide = Write on the INVOICE, asked as the caller (D-77). No caller-token write reaches sprk_billingevent. A caller without Write gets 403 and nothing is read or written (strict mock). A right on another invoice does not count, and a failed rights check is denied (N1).</criterion>
    <criterion>uac A3: NoFirm, HeldForFirm and RerunPending each give 409 ebilling.line_add.firm_missing with nothing written and no SignalWriter or recorder call (N3). Each closed status (Approved, Rejected, Returned to Firm, Superseded, Sent to AP, Paid) gives 409 ebilling.invoice.not_in_review (N4). The 403 and 404 are the uniform ones, and every refusal carries errorCode.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac A4: internal only. Callers with FlagTrue, with NoSystemUserRow, and on the CiamContact plane are refused before any rights call or read (N2). Seed S4 shows that removing RequireInternalFinanceCaller fails that test.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac A5: a missing, blank or too-long reason gives 400 before any read (N5). The record names the caller.</criterion>
    <criterion>Input checks: every other 400 code in brief section 3 (N6); an out-of-set code is refused and never stored; an unresolvable code set gives 409.</criterion>
    <criterion>Idempotency (N7): repeating the same requestId with the same content gives 200 alreadyApplied with one row, one record and no new Signal episode. The same requestId with different content gives 409 id_reused.</criterion>
    <criterion>Concurrency (N8): a submission or invoice version changed between the read and the commit gives 409 ebilling.line_add.changed with no row, no record and no Signal. A held lock gives 409 busy. A test proves that the version-only invoice condition is honoured.</criterion>
    <criterion>Refusals (N9, N11): a new Procedure gap gives 409 procedure_gap; an unapplied correction gives 409 corrections_pending; an unresolved owner gives 500. Each writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion>Recovery (N10): a fault at totals, record or signals gives 503 ebilling.decision.incomplete with failedStep. The repeat completes it, and exactly one record exists.</criterion>
    <criterion>Seeds S1-S4 (brief section 8) are recorded in the notes. Only access and fail-open guards are seeded.</criterion>
    <criterion>Guards G1-G5 pass, including the unchanged correction suites, the FindingsJson reviewed list with its notes/122 row, the ParentLineage text, and the census entry.</criterion>
    <criterion>Client: C1-C4 pass. The form is FormModal (ADR-050). The client validates nothing the server owns. The button shows only when canDecide is true and the invoice is In Review.</criterion>
    <criterion>Ribbon: the dry run lists the hides (Mscrm.HomepageGrid.sprk_billingevent.NewRecord, Mscrm.SubGrid.sprk_billingevent.AddNewStandard, Mscrm.Form.sprk_billingevent.NewRecord and .SaveAndNew, plus any SubGrid NewRecord present) and writes nothing. It refuses while non-live sprk.SecureChild.* ids are in the diff (P1). -Verify exits 0 or 1 (P2). -Apply is not run.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: exactly brief section 8 (T1-T8, N1-N11, S1-S4, G1-G5, C1-C4, P1-P2). Anything beyond needs a one-line reason in notes/164-add-line.md.</criterion>
    <criterion>Gate:
      - the test projects build;
      - ArchTests and the filtered suites (Finance, Signals, InvoiceReview, Corrections) pass;
      - npm build:prod and vitest pass for InvoiceReview;
      - the publish delta is measured against a fresh master build;
      - the PR states the placement and the §11 answers (brief sections 6, 7).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A new column or table is needed (for example, the owner rejects Q2's JSON marker), or any schema change. STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>An ADR conflict, for example a second owner of a line invariant (ADR-002) or a job being needed (ADR-052). Stop and use root CLAUDE.md 6.5.</trigger>
    <trigger>The rule evaluator cannot be run for the new line through the whole-invoice before/after diff: a fact the new line needs cannot be built without an AI read, or the diff cannot isolate the new line's and the total rules' findings. STOP and list it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Dataverse does not honour the version-only conditional invoice update. STOP and propose an alternative.</trigger>
    <trigger>The design needs a persister edit, an AI call, an external route, a SignalWriter contract change, or a new Decision Record writer entry point beyond the Q3 line-code addition. STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>Q1-Q4 are unanswered when 164a starts, or Q6 is unanswered before -Apply. STOP.</trigger>
  </escalation>

